author: pm-github
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: "Use the pinned public SDK global-option contract and refuse ambiguous resolution; Real source and built HTTP collision acceptance returns 409 with no execution marker and unchanged settings for both separate-value cases; Cover equals forms, nested flag positions, booleans and terminators while preserving owned commands; Behavioral helper revert fails after rebuilding and both release gates pass at unchanged thresholds"
comments[9]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-12T10:53:15.064Z",codex-sol,"Imported only issue 189 with published pm-github using a since filter after a one-issue dry run; atomic privacy-gated import created one item with GitHub provenance. The CLI lacks an issue-number filter. Plan: reproduce the unchanged helper against real pinned CLI receipts, use the public SDK bootstrap contract, and extend source/built HTTP collision acceptance. Publication boundary: affected current source follows the published Web tarball; no hosted or published Web exposure asserted."
  "2026-10-12T10:54:35.323Z",codex-sol,"Exact issue reproduction passed: script-disabled official CLI 2026.10.10 in a scratch tracker with synthetic pm-presets priority 1 and scratch-shadow priority 1000. Unchanged extracted helper SHA-256 ae77965435324d7bf16273f86d580a193c75f3c747927f1bc3dbe19bdeb6668c refused plain list and author equals, but allowed separate-value author and output-format while actual CLI selected scratch-shadow in both cases. Real describe receipt supplied; only process transport replaced. Additional dispatch probe confirms a terminator before list keeps the base owner; list before a terminator selects the nested shadow."
  "2026-10-12T10:56:42.861Z",codex-sol,"HTTP acceptance exposed a further in-scope terminator ambiguity: published Presets interprets operands after -- and can dispatch its nested shadow, unlike the minimal synthetic base handler. Refuse terminators carrying operands when exact secondary resolution is unavailable; empty trailing terminators and ordinary owned local boolean flags remain supported. Unknown local option arity with later operands also fails closed. Tests exercise real npm Presets and both source/built applications."
  "2026-10-12T10:59:08.313Z",codex-sol,"Focused HTTP acceptance passes 3/3 (built and source collision flows plus SSE deadline test), with zero skips. Matrix proves real CLI shadow execution, HTTP 409 with no shadow marker and byte-identical settings, separate and equals author/output-format options before and after list, boolean flags, fail-closed ambiguous operands, and owned-command restoration. Lint, zero-duplication, docstring, and changelog regeneration/check pass. Behavioral revert now replaces only commandOwnershipError with its original implementation and rebuilds before rerunning unchanged tests."
  "2026-10-12T11:00:00.095Z",codex-sol,"Behavioral revert proof: replaced only commandOwnershipError with baseline source, kept all tests and imports, rebuilt dist, and ran node scripts/with-test-db.ts node --test test/catalog-install-e2e.test.ts. Result: 3 executed, 1 passed, 2 failed, 0 skipped. Both built and source flows failed the separate-value author assertion: HTTP 200 with scratch-shadow output instead of 409. No syntax or module-load failures. Restored the fixed helper and rebuilt dist; running PM-linked acceptance and both full release gates next."
  "2026-10-12T11:19:49.275Z",codex-sol,"npm run release:check passes with isolated HOME and global/system Git config disabled: 575/575 tests, 0 failures/skips, 34 configured sources, statements/lines 90.54%, branches 80.47%, functions 93.45%, unchanged thresholds 90/90/79/92. Production audit 0 vulnerabilities, zero duplication, typechecks/lint/docstrings pass, all four packed npm/Bun current/minimum-host scenarios pass, changelog and release attestation/date checks pass. Restored PM-linked acceptance passes 3/3. Bun release gate is running on the same runtime/test source."
  "2026-10-12T11:29:28.159Z",codex-sol,"First Bun release-gate attempt passed both ownership HTTP flows but hit the existing graph latency flake: 2000-item read 10277 ms wall against unchanged 10000 ms, 3192 ms CPU and 9061 involuntary context switches. The passing npm gate measured 2365 ms wall for the same assertion. Existing follow-up pm-web-hqqp owns this separate scheduling/performance discrepancy. Retain the failure receipt and rerun the complete Bun gate without changing source, thresholds, or the latency bound."
  "2026-10-12T11:34:30.408Z",codex-sol,"First Bun gate complete: 573/575 pass, 2 failures, 0 skips, exit 1. Failures are the existing graph wall-time bound (pm-web-hqqp) and independent-child startup overlap assertion (pm-web-qdhx); both ownership flows passed. Retained failed-gate evidence. Starting a fresh isolated-HOME full Bun gate without any runtime/test/threshold changes."
  "2026-10-12T11:52:01.360Z",codex-sol,"Final full Bun release gate passes after an unchanged retry: 575/575, zero failures/skips, all 34 configured sources, statements/lines 90.61%, branches 80.62%, functions 93.45%, unchanged 90/90/79/92 thresholds. All four packed npm/Bun current/minimum-host scenarios, production audit (0), zero duplication, typechecks/lint/docstrings, changelog, release-date and attestation checks pass. Both passing gates pack identical local candidate tarballs with SHA-1 d3184c08bc542634a5666e3628fc0d8865d66694. Earlier Bun 573/575 failure remains documented on existing pm-web-hqqp and pm-web-qdhx. Runtime/test source and dependency pins were unchanged between attempts. Ready for PR on fix/gh189-ownership-global-flags; item stays in progress. No deployment or publication."
